## std.env — environment variable lookup.
##
## From docs/spec.md §6.4 (System Surfaces): get_env returns `?str`
## (None if the variable is unset).
##
## v0.1 Tier-1 migration: real impl (renamed from `getEnv` to
## snake_case per the method-naming convention). The body is written
## entirely in zag, backed by the always-emitted `__zag_getenv`
## preamble helper (src/codegen/core.zig) — a self-contained
## /proc/self/environ scanner with no zig-stdlib env dependency. The
## helper takes `[]const u8` so the call site passes `name` directly
## (no sentinel-terminated stack buffer, no `as [*:0]const u8` cast —
## a single pointer cannot @as-cast into a many-pointer in zig 0.16).
##
## The `?str` contract: a non-null result is a slice into the
## process-owned env block (docs/11 borrowed-string-view) — users
## wanting heap ownership must copy or `String.from_slice` on the
## borrowed view before it ceases to be valid.
##
## Router history: the pre-migration `env_var` router row in
## src/codegen/builtins.zig emitted a per-call
## `blk: { break :blk @as(?[]const u8, std.posix.getenv(...)); }`
## shim. Retired in the Tier-1 migration — this real .zag body is
## the single source of truth (matches the std.fs.read_file
## migration pattern).

pub fun get_env(name: str) -> ?str {
    return __zag_getenv(name);
}
